  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted) achieved 0.532 acc, while config_050 (rna_only, same RNA encoder/profile) achieved 0.485 acc, a ~4.7% gap. However, we cannot yet decompose whether this gain comes from the image modality alone or from the synergy of combining both modalities. Question: config_022 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) provides a clean three-way comparison (RNA-only vs. image-only vs. multimodal) with only the model_setting changed from config_005, isolating the contribution of the RNA branch. Why best next: This is the most fundamental uncertainty—whether multimodal fusion is actually adding value beyond the stronger single modality, or whether one modality dominates. The answer directly determines whether to invest remaining budget in fusion/aggregation design (if synergy exists) or in improving the single dominant modality (if one modality suffices). No other single experiment reduces as much downstream uncertainty under the limited budget."
}

